Time out a half-open connection before accept returns.

A peer that sends a SYN and never answers the SYN-ACK held the
listening socket in SYN-RECEIVED for good, because smoltcp
retransmits the SYN-ACK with no retry limit and the socket had no
timeout until accept returned. Each such peer cost the server one
listener, until none was left. A timeout set on the acceptor now
reaches each socket before it listens.

